\begin{abstractwithpageno}	
International School Manila manages sponsorship billing and Letter of Guarantee (LoG) coverage across four independent systems—PowerSchool (SIS), Student Charging Portal (SCP), NetSuite (ERP), and the Online Billing System (OBS)—that lack a unified decision point. Manual interpretation of LoG provisions at charge entry produces inconsistent Bill-To assignments, reversals, and weak audit trails, which in turn complicate compliance with the Bureau of Internal Revenue’s Ease of Paying Taxes (EoPT) requirements. This project proposes and prototypes a Sponsor Management and LoG Coverage Integration System that centralizes sponsor master data and encodes deterministic LoG rules, then evaluates coverage at the moment of charge entry. The system exposes a real-time decision interface (Covered, Split, or Not Covered), computes authoritative Bill-To and sponsor–parent allocations, and records a complete, time-stamped audit log. The pilot was implemented as an ASP.NET Core progressive web application on Microsoft Azure with Azure SQL Database, Azure AD authentication including Google OAuth for staff, and REST APIs documented via Swagger/OpenAPI. Comprehensive testing validated security (10 vulnerabilities identified and remediated via OWASP ZAP scanning), performance (sub-200ms coverage evaluation response time), and functional correctness (86.4% pass rate across 110 test cases). The pilot demonstrates reduced manual interpretation, deterministic coverage decisions, improved audit trails, and a foundation for production integration with PowerSchool, NetSuite, and OBS. The work contributes a practical integration pattern for institutions that must preserve existing platforms while achieving consistent, explainable coverage and EoPT-aligned documentation.

\end{abstractwithpageno}